    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пожалуйста, поговори с папой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Please talk to dad.' Max combines 'please' with 'dad' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Nastya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Я постараюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will try.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'I' with 'to try'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А что это такое?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what is this?' Max combines 'and' with 'on earth' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Это мой десерт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is my dessert.' Notice how 'this' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'dessert'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Прямо как у шефа.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Just like the Chef's.' Max links 'right' directly with 'how' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Спасибо большое.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you very much.' The character links 'thank you' directly with 'big' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Можно попробовать?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can I taste it?' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'may' with 'to taste'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "valya",
      "t": "Конечно, бери.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course, take it.' The character uses the imperative command form of the verb meaning 'take'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is very tasty.' The first content word means 'this', and 'it's tasty' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nastya",
      "t": "Да, мне тоже нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I like it too.' Nastya links 'yes' directly with 'to me' to express the thought clearly.",
